<title>UK: Brent crude cargo trades at Dec Brent -6 cents.</title>
<headline>Brent crude cargo trades at Dec Brent -6 cents.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A cargo of Brent crude, scheduled to load in the November 7-9 range, traded on Monday at December Brent -6 cents, the equivalent of November -33 cents, traders said.</p>
<p>This was for a maximum size cargo and some 13 cents below trade on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;This market is dumping. Brent was kept up high last week and now everyone can see that no one wants it. It was well overpriced (last week),&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>--Siobhan Hayden, London Newsroom +44 71 542 8978</p>
